   \[
   \text{Weight in kg} = \frac{\text{Weight in lbs}}{2.205} = \frac{32 \text{ lbs}}{2.205} \approx 14.4 \text{ kg}
   \]

2. Calculate the total load dose in kilograms:
   \[
   \text{Load dose in kg} = 20 \text{ mg/kg} \times 14.4 \text{ kg} = 288 \text{ mg}
   \]

