However, if we assume that the concentration of the compound in the sample of diluted water is 0.0125 M, and the concentration of the compound in the original diluted water sample is what we are looking for, we can use the mass balance principle to find the concentration of the compound in the original diluted water sample.

The mass balance equation is:

\[
\text{Concentration in original solution} \times \text{Volume of original solution} = \text{Concentency in combined solution} \times \text{Volume of combined solution}
\]

