The negation of the proposition ""If $A \cup B = A$, then $A \cap B = B$"" is __________.
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The negation of the proposition ""If $A \cup B = A$, then $A \cap B = B$"" is:

$$ \neg (A \cup B = A \rightarrow A \cap B = B) $$

The negation of an implication $p \rightarrow q$ is $p \land \neg q$. Applying this to our proposition, we get:

$$ A \cup B = A \land \neg (A \cap B = B) $$

This can be written as:

$$ A \cup B = A \land (A \cap B \neq B) $$

Thus, the negation of the given proposition is:
$$ A \cup B = A \land (A \cap B \neq B) $$

This means that $A \cup B = A$ and $A \cap B \neq B$.
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

