   - If \( n(n+1) \) is a perfect power, say \( a^b \), then both \( n \) and \( n+1 \) must be perfect powers (possibly with \( b = 1 \)), but since \( b > 1 \), \( n \) and \( n+1 \) must be perfect powers.

