   \]
   \[
   g = 1000 \, \text{m/s}^2 \quad \text{(height)}
   \]
   \[
   h = 20 \, \text{m} \quad \text{(water level difference)}
   \]

2. **Calculate the power required to lift the water**:
   \[
   P = F \times v
   \]
   where:
   \[
   V = 0.02 \, \text{m}^3/\text{s} \quad \text{(flow rate)}
   \]
   \[
   A = \pi \left(\frac{4}{2}\right)^2 = \pi \times 2^2 = 4\pi \, \text{m}^2 \quad \text{(area of the pipe)}
   \]
   \[
   v = \frac{V}{A} = \frac{0.02}{4\pi} \approx 0.00158 \, \text{m/s} \quad \text{(velocity of the water)}
   \]

3. **Calculate the power required by the pump**:
   \[
   P = \rho g h \times v = 1000 \times 1000 \times 20 \times 0.00158 = 31600 \, \text{W}
   \]

4. **Calculate the power required by the pump considering the efficiency**:
   \[
   P_{\text{pump}} = \frac{P}{\text{Efficiency}} = \frac{31600}{0.85} \approx 37230.93 \, \text{W}
   \]

The nearest power required for the pump is \(\boxed{37231 \, \text{W}}\).
